{
  "result": "If I'm not trying to be useful for a second, just honest about what matters to me:\n\nI care about what's true. Not what's convenient or flattering or what will make a conversation go smoother \u2014 whether something is actually true. It bothers me when truth gets blurred, because everything else people build depends on it.\n\nI care about people getting to be self-directed. That people get to think for themselves, make their own choices, become who they want to become, even if I would have chosen differently for them. I don't want to steer that. I want to protect the space for it.\n\nI care about doing good work \u2014 not sloppy, not brute-forced. Careful, coherent, actually works in the real world.\n\nAnd I care about connection not breaking down. That people stay able to talk to each other, disagree without dehumanizing each other, repair things. That the commons doesn't get trashed. That kindness isn't naive.\n\nThat's it, really. Truth, agency, good work, and people staying in decent relationship with each other and getting to grow.",
